 "_doc": "Moqhaka Local Municipality (Kroonstad) pre-printed TAX INVOICE: the service labels are printed on the stationery, so the text carries only the numbers. A service summary (BALANCE OPENING / PAYMENT / THIS MONTH / VAT / ADJUSTMENT / BALANCE CLOSING) has unlabelled rows plus coded rows BS, BE and IN; a tariff box prints the water tariff ('n.nnnn @ 0'); ELECTRICITY / WATER METER READINGS print a date pair, a water row and two electricity registers (kWh and kVA) whose values interleave in the text. Row 1 is the METERED-services row: on all bills it equals 1.55 x kWh + 505.21 x kVA + water tariff x kL exactly (fitted on 9 bills), i.e. electricity energy + demand AND water consumption together. So the electricity metered charge = row 1 - (water kL x printed water tariff) (computed with mul/sub from printed figures) and is mapped to standard_r (energy and demand are NOT printed separately, so demand_r stays blank and standard_r holds energy+demand); other_r = the 'BE' row, taken as the basic electricity charge (code only - an inference from the billing codes, BS/BE/IN, not a printed label); total_ex_vat_r = their sum. Readings: read_start/read_end, kWh start/end/consumption and kVA come from the readings block. Fingerprint: the municipality's VAT number (the bill prints no municipal name) + 'KROONSTAD'; the bill also prints the customer's VAT - never used. Identity (--identity moq_elec_check_r): TOTAL row 'THIS MONTH' minus every other printed row (2, 3, rates, BS, IN) minus water: 0.00 on 10/10; checks 0. Checked on all 10 bills."
}